 them."},{"id":"led-r2-q3","version":2,"round":2,"type":"mc","prompt":"Which statement about an LED's structure is right?","options":["It is a reverse-biased junction that emits when it breaks down","It is a MOS capacitor in inversion","It is a silicon diode with a coloured lens","It is a forward-biased pn junction of a direct-gap material, packaged with a lens to collect and direct the light"],"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Forward bias injects minority carriers, which recombine radiatively in the direct-gap material; the lens collimates the output.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"LED symbol: a forward-biased diode with arrows showing light emitted from the junction.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:300px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"112\" y2=\"60\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"60\"/><polygon points=\"112,52 112,68 128,60\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"128\" y2=\"68\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"14\"/><polygon points=\"180,14 176.9,20.3 173.3,16.2\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"18\"/><polygon points=\"200,18 196.9,24.3 193.3,20.2\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">forward current</text><text x=\"212\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">light</text></svg>","figure_alt":"LED symbol: a forward-biased diode with arrows showing light emitted from the junction."},{"id":"led-r3-q1","round":3,"type":"numeric","prompt":"An LED draws \\(20\\ \\mathrm{mA}\\). If 30% of injected electrons recombine radiatively and every photon escapes, how many photons per second are emitted?","answer":3.74532e+16,"unit":"photons/s","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"Electrons per second \\(= I/q = 1.25\\times10^{17}\\); 30% of them give photons: \\(3.7\\times10^{16}\\ \\mathrm{s^{-1}}\\).","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 350 190\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Direct band gap E-k diagram: the conduction-band minimum sits directly above the valence-band maximum, so a vertical (photon-only) transition connects them.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:350px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"170\"/><polygon points=\"330,170 323.6,172.7 323.6,167.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"20\"/><polygon points=\"40,20 42.7,26.4 37.3,26.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">k</text><text x=\"44\" y=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">E</text><polyline points=\"125,84.4 126.5,83.7 128,83 129.5,82.3 131,81.7 132.5,81 134,80.4 135.5,79.8 137,79.2 138.5,78.6 140,78.1 141.5,77.6 143,77.1 144.5,76.6 146,76.1 147.5,75.6 149,75.2 150.5,74.8 152,74.4 153.5,74 155,73.6 156.5,73.2 158,72.9 159.5,72.6 161,72.3 162.5,72 164,71.8 165.5,71.5 167,71.3 168.5,71.1 170,70.9 171.5,70.7 173,70.6 174.5,70.4 176,70.3 177.5,70.2 179,70.1 180.5,70.1 182,70 183.5,70 185,70 186.5,70 188,70 189.5,70.1 191,70.1 192.5,70.2 194,70.3 195.5,70.4 197,70.6 198.5,70.7 200,70.9 201.5,71.1 203,71.3 204.5,71.5 206,71.8 207.5,72 209,72.3 210.5,72.6 212,72.9 213.5,73.2 215,73.6 216.5,74 218,74.4 219.5,74.8 221,75.2 222.5,75.6 224,76.1 225.5,76.6 227,77.1 228.5,77.6 230,78.1 231.5,78.6 233,79.2 234.5,79.8 236,80.4 237.5,81 239,81.7 240.5,82.3 242,83 243.5,83.7 245,84.4\"/><polyline points=\"125,125.6 126.5,126.3 128,127 129.5,127.7 131,128.3 132.5,129 134,129.6 135.