olour follows that wavelength: visible light is roughly 400 to 700 nm, and a longer wavelength is infrared.","variables":[{"name":"h","min":0.2,"max":4.0},{"name":"c","min":0.2,"max":6.0},{"name":"lam","min":0.2,"max":5.0}],"alternates":["h*(c/lam)","(h*c)/lam"]},{"id":"led-r4-q1","round":4,"type":"mc","prompt":"Preview of the diode equation: an LED's light output rises roughly in proportion to its current. How does the needed forward voltage change if the current is raised tenfold?","options":["It rises tenfold","It rises only by about \\(V_{th}\\ln 10\\) (roughly 60 mV for an ideal diode)","It falls","It must reach the band-gap voltage times ten"],"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Current is exponential in voltage, so a decade of current costs only about 60 mV (ideal).","preview":["diode-ss"],"figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 350 190\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Direct band gap E-k diagram: the conduction-band minimum sits directly above the valence-band maximum, so a vertical (photon-only) transition connects them.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:350px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"170\"/><polygon points=\"330,170 323.6,172.7 323.6,167.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"20\"/><polygon points=\"40,20 42.7,26.4 37.3,26.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">k</text><text x=\"44\" y=\"16\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">E</text><polyline points=\"125,84.4 126.5,83.7 128,83 129.5,82.3 131,81.7 132.5,81 134,80.4 135.5,79.8 137,79.2 138.5,78.6 140,78.1 141.5,77.6 143,77.1 144.5,76.6 146,76.1 147.5,75.6 149,75.2 150.5,74.8 152,74.4 153.5,74 155,73.6 156.5,73.2 158,72.9 159.5,72.6 161,72.3 162.5,72 16